From 86dda7e4a7f4b6b3818f2e3575d1fbf991fddf3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:52:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 846/913] drivers: stm32_risab: save/restore context regardless
 of CID role

The RISAB power management callback returned early without saving or
restoring the RISAB configuration when the core was not the trusted
domain CID (is_tdcid). The RISAB1/2 handle the Sysram which is only
accessible by A35 even when the M33 is TDCID. As a result, on M33TD,
the RISAB1/2 are not restored on resume from a Standby.

Remove the !is_tdcid condition so that the context is always saved on
suspend and restored on resume in case of a standby sequence.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 8a5f4a58370f5f2415b83b6ff37591eb2799704c drivers: stm32_risab: save/restore context regardless of CID role]
Fixes: c413678c6ca6 ("drivers: stm32_risab: add RISAB internal memory firewall driver")
Change-Id: I588b05e72fba73a471e980d48653346dfc9c770c
Signed-off-by: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/598708
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risab.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risab.c b/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risab.c
index 0c37b4332..def9ca9a9 100644
--- a/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risab.c
+++ b/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risab.c
@@ -817,7 +817,7 @@ stm32_risab_pm(enum pm_op op, unsigned int pm_hint,
 	struct stm32_risab_pdata *risab = pm_handle->handle;
 	TEE_Result res = TEE_ERROR_GENERIC;
 
-	if (!PM_HINT_IS_STATE(pm_hint, CONTEXT) || !is_tdcid)
+	if (!PM_HINT_IS_STATE(pm_hint, CONTEXT))
 		return TEE_SUCCESS;
 
 	if (op == PM_OP_RESUME)
-- 
